    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Owen Reilly present 47 Larkfield Gardens, a beautifully refurbished red brick family home situated in a quiet and well-established residential setting in Harold's Cross. Dating from the 1930s, this charming property successfully combines original character with stylish modern upgrades, offering an excellent opportunity for first-time buyers, growing families, or those looking to downsize while remaining in the local area.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation (in total 96 sq. m. including attic room of 16 sq. m ) begins with a welcoming entrance hall leading to a bright open-plan living room, originally two separate reception rooms, which flows seamlessly into the kitchen and breakfast room, creating a practical and sociable living space. The breakfast room opens directly onto a generous walled rear garden, enjoying a sunny west-facing aspect with excellent privacy, making it an ideal setting for outdoor dining, entertaining, or simply relaxing.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, the first floor features three bedrooms, including two generous double bedrooms and a single bedroom, together with a stylishly upgraded family bathroom. The converted attic provides valuable additional accommodation, ideal as a home office, hobby room, playroom, or for extra storage.\r\n\r\nTo the front, the property benefits from an attractive lawned garden bordered by mature hedging, providing privacy and kerb appeal. Ample resident parking is available.\r\n\r\n47 Larkfield Gardens offers a wonderful combination of period charm, modern comfort, and an enviable location, with excellent access to nearby villages, local amenities, parks, schools, and Dublin city centre.\r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended.\r\n\r\nMore about the location...\r\n\r\nLarkfield is a mature and quiet residential area within easy reach of several popular villages, including Harold's Cross, Kimmage, Terenure, and Rathgar. These areas provide a wide range of amenities including shops, cafés, restaurants, schools, and local services. Nearby highlights include Sundrive SuperValu, Zero Zero Pizza, and Le Petit Renard.\r\n\r\nThere are also excellent recreational facilities in the area, with nearby green spaces including Harold's Cross Park, Bushy Park, and Eamonn Ceannt Park, all within walking distance.\r\n\r\nThe area is very well served by public transport. Numerous bus routes operate close by on Larkfield Park (S2, 83, 83A), as well as along Kimmage Road Lower and Harold’s Cross Road, providing convenient access to the Dublin City Centre and further destinations across the city."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall (4.67m x 1.62m)\r\nWelcoming entrance hall with a tiled floor and decorative dado rail, setting the tone for the well-presented accommodation throughout.\r\n\r\nLiving Room (6.88m x 3.13m)\r\nBright and spacious open-plan reception room, created by combining two original reception rooms to form an impressive living and dining area. Features include a cast iron open fireplace, built-in alcove cabinetry and polished timber floorboards, adding warmth and character.\r\n\r\nKitchen (4.35m x 2.35m)\r\nWell-appointed kitchen fitted with an excellent range of wall and floor units, complemented by solid wood worktops and a tiled splashback. Integrated appliances include a five-ring gas hob, electric oven and extractor fan. Plumbed for both a dishwasher and washing machine. Finished with striking black and white chequered floor tiles.\r\n\r\n\r\nBreakfast Room (2.49m x 2.13m)\r\nBright breakfast area adjoining the kitchen, featuring a pitched ceiling with a Velux roof window, recessed lighting and double doors opening directly onto the rear garden. An ideal space for everyday dining and entertaining.\r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 (3.59m x 2.83m)\r\nGenerous double bedroom overlooking the rear garden, complete with built-in wardrobes and an attractive cast iron fireplace.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 (2.59m x 2.88m)\r\nBright double bedroom to the front with two built-in alcove wardrobes providing excellent storage.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 (2.59m x 1.96m)\r\nSingle bedroom overlooking the front, suitable for use as a child’s bedroom, home office, or study.\r\n\r\nBathroom (1.95m x 1.94m)\r\nStylishly appointed and extensively tiled, comprising a bath with overhead shower, WC and wash hand basin set within a vanity unit. Heated towel rail.\r\n\r\nAttic Room (4.91m x 3.26m)\r\nConverted attic room with a pitched ceiling and three large Velux roof windows, allowing for excellent natural light. Finished with timber flooring and useful eaves storage, offering a versatile space suitable as a home office, hobby room or additional storage.\r\n\r\nALL MEASUREMENTS ARE APPROXIMATE AND FOR GUIDANCE PURPOSES ONLY."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Attractive red brick mid-terrace family home.\r\nBeautifully refurbished and extended throughout.\r\nBright, spacious open-plan living accommodation at ground floor level.\r\nContemporary kitchen with excellent storage and workspace.\r\nThree well-proportioned bedrooms plus a converted attic room.\r\nStylishly upgraded family bathroom.\r\nRetains many original period features, including cast iron fireplaces, panelled doors and original brass door furniture.\r\nDouble-glazed windows throughout, upgraded in 2023, including attractive sash-style windows to the front elevation.\r\nExcellent built-in storage throughout the property\r\n80 sq. m of accommodation plus an additional 16 sq. m attic conversion.\r\nGas-fired central heating with boiler replaced in 2021.\r\nLarge private west-facing rear garden 18m / 59 ft. , not overlooked from the rear.\r\nAttractive front garden with mature hedging providing additional privacy.\r\nAmple on-street resident parking.\r\nQuiet, mature residential setting in this highly sought-after Dublin 6W location.\r\nWithin easy reach of Harold’s Cross, Terenure and Rathgar villages, with excellent local amenities, schools, parks and transport links.\r\nConvenient access to Dublin city centre."
      },
